{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Navigate the bound Noobscape session to `url` IN PLACE: evals location.assign() in the driven tab and polls until the new document's readyState settles (a planted token on the old document marks the swap; the same-document hash/SPA-route case is recognized by href match). Works because the mechanism evaluates under AutoEntryScript — script-initiated navigation commits — and the bind latch keys on the tab's stable BrowserId, so the eval channel follows the tab across a cross-process swap. The browser process, profile, and history survive; only the old document's JS state resets, as any real navigation would. Falls back to the legacy rebind (close + relaunch at `url`) when no session answers or the load never commits. Returns {status, pid, url}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;","params":[{"name":"url","type":"String"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"tzwzqk1a03b80b9a5zc","readers":[],"time":1788623611662,"username":"system","writers":[]}